   "text": {
    "L1": "Floods happen when more water comes than a river, drain, or ground can hold.",
    "L2": "Very heavy rain, overflowing rivers, and blocked drains can bring floods.",
    "L3": "Tree roots and grass hold soil and help rain soak into the ground.",
    "L4": "When forests are cut, rain runs off fast with mud, so floods can come quicker.",
    "L5": "Sewage, factory waste, garbage, plastic, soap, and harmful idols make rivers dirty.",
    "L6": "A river cannot clean away everything. Plastic and harmful chemicals stay and hurt living things downstream.",
    "L7": "We can keep drains clear, keep waste out of water, use clay idols, and plant trees.",
    "L8": "In a flood, stay away from flowing water and follow official warnings.",
    "L9": "Tap the actions that help prevent floods and keep rivers clean."
   },
